cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  dnsjax: a GPU-accelerated pseudo-spectral solver for direct numerical
  simulation of the incompressible Navier-Stokes equations
message: If dnsjax supports your work, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Gökhan
    family-names: Yalnız
repository-code: https://github.com/gokhanyalniz/dnsjax
url: https://github.com/gokhanyalniz/dnsjax
abstract: >-
  dnsjax integrates the three-dimensional incompressible Navier-Stokes
  equations by a pseudo-spectral treatment of the periodic directions
  combined with banded finite differences in up to one wall-bounded
  direction, where an influence-matrix method reconciles
  incompressibility with the wall boundary conditions. Written in JAX,
  it runs on CPUs, GPUs and TPUs, on a single device or sharded across
  many, in single or double precision.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - direct numerical simulation
  - turbulence
  - pseudo-spectral method
  - Navier-Stokes equations
  - JAX
  - GPU computing
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
